{"_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"content": "Peter's Dating Misadventures", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "How Have You Been?", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 4, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 8, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "B1.3", "type": "level"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"content": "  Exchange information about people's interests and backgrounds using a wider range of language.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": " Understands important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": " Understands important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": " Understands important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": " Understands important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": " Understands important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": " Understands important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": " Understands important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": " Understands important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"content": "engenn8le08ob04re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": " The Silent h Sound", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You don't say every letter in a word in English pronunciation. Some letters are silent, which means that you don't hear them as you would pronounce them normally.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "In words like <span class=\"italic\">honest</span>, <span class=\"italic\">hour</span>, or <span class=\"italic\">honor</span>, the letter <span class=\"italic\">h </span>is silent.<br /> In words like <span class=\"italic\">character</span> or <span class=\"italic\">choir</span>, the letter <span class=\"italic\">h </span>is also silent. It does not combine with another consonant to produce a consonant blend. <br /><br /> Here are examples of the silent letter <span class=\"italic\">h</span> in words. Practice saying the example sentences.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":7,\"columns\":3,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Letter\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Words\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Pronunciation\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Silent h\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\"> honest </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"onest\\\"}\",\"\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\"> hour </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"our\\\"}\",\"\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\"> psychic </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"psykic\\\"}\",\"\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\"> choir </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"kwire\\\"}\",\"\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\"> echo </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"eko\\\"}\",\"\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\"> whisper </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"wisper\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\"\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": "To be honest, I have no idea anymore.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "So last week I decided to see a psychic.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "That sounds totally out of character! ", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": " Linking and Deletion with Must  ", "type": "heading"}, {"content": " When a word ending in consonant +/t/ links into a word beginning with a consonant, the final /t/ of the first word is often deleted. This is often the case with the word must.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "When you delete (or drop) the final /t/, the sound before the /t/ must link smoothly into the following word. <br /><br /> You must be happy= You mus_be happy<br /><br />  When the word <span class=\"italic\">have</span> follows <span class=\"italic\">must</span>,  have is reduced to \"_ov\" or \"_av\". The 't' sound joins the reduced have.<br /><br />  must have   =  mus_tuv or mus_tav <br /><br />  Practice saying the words in the chart.<br /><br />", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":4,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\"><span class=\\\"strong\\\"> Phrase </span> </div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\"><span class=\\\"strong\\\"> Pronunciation </span> </div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" must find\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"mus_find\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" must be\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"mus_be\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" must have thought\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"mus_tuv thought<br /> mus_ta thought\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\"\"}", "type": "table"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "out of character ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "it refers to a person acting out his usual behavior", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Are you serious? That sounds totally out of character!", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le08ob04aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": " These are words you hear and use in social situations.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "honest ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "used to describe a person who is honorable in principles, intentions, and actions", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: To be honest, I have no idea anymore.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le08ob04aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "psychic ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a person who is allegedly sensitive to psychic influences or forces", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Anyway, was the psychic right in the end?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le08ob04aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "choir ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a company of singers or an organized group of voices", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I followed her advice and joined a choir.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le08ob04aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to echo", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to sound repetitively by the reflection of sound wave", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I love how our voices echo in that huge space.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le08ob04aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to whisper", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to speak or say with soft, quiet, hushed sounds", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: She whispered in my ear when we were singing.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le08ob04aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "Pretend that you are telling someone how to take a flight.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Using \u201cmust\u201d, write at least ten steps explaining how to go through airport security and board the flight (e.g. <span class=\"italic\">You mustn't bring bottles of liquid, You must check your bags at the counter</span>).", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Present your list to your partner.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "I create a step-by-step list", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I give directions using must and mustn't", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I present my instructions to a partner", "type": "text"}]}], "labs": [{"exercises": [{"questions": [], "template_override": 1, "img_path": "", "stimuli_ids": [0], "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"content": "I can say and use words like character.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " I can speculate about things, people and events. ", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " I can stress new information.